# Build context of the twelve service images (docker-compose.yml builds each with
# `context: .`, and ci.yml's image-versus-lock check builds ai-orchestrator from the
# same directory). Everything is left out, then only the paths the service
# Dockerfiles COPY are let back in, so the context never carries VCS data,
# virtualenvs, local env files, generated keys and certificates, or local folders.
# tests/unit/test_dockerignore.py fails when a COPY source is excluded.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!services
!docs/manual

# Inside the paths let back in: virtualenvs, caches, test and coverage output,
# node packages, build output, env files, keys, certificates, and editor files.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov*
**/coverage*.xml
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
